    "updated_at": "2026-11-15T23:39:02Z",
    "body": "Escalated from effort:high to effort:max. Claim released.\n\nThe finer-contact reproduction fails on upstream/main 31f8d03d without a production change.\nTest: box_refuses_sub_pitch_side_face_overlap_at_four_grid_phases and mesh_refuses_sub_pitch_side_face_overlap_at_four_grid_phases both fail.\nBoth checks pass 0.05 mm penetration at phases [0.1, 0.3, 0.7, 0.9] on a 1 mm grid.\nContact and 0.05 mm clearance controls pass.\nCommand: cargo test -p camcraft-app --test carried_fixture_side_contact -- --nocapture.\nFailure log: /tmp/1580-side-red.log on this machine.\n\nThe box scan reads column centres. The mesh check between columns reads only material that four columns share.\nNeither check identifies the stock boundary inside a cell. Body::on_mesh also discards continuous history.\nA general fix needs a new boundary-intersection or refinement algorithm for side faces and steps.\nThe effort table assigns new geometry and collision algorithms to effort:max.\n\nI did not expand the columns into cells. That change can refuse valid face contact.\nMore fixture-mesh samples do not recover the missing stock boundary.\nThe earlier bound-only tests passed unchanged. They do not meet the required red-before-fix rule.\n\nHeld work: mkinney:issue/1580-carried-side-contact at 33cc6fa8165728bbf1e306a68e59e46fadff1444.\nThe branch contains a reproduction and a decision record. It contains no production fix.\nNo PR was opened. No goldens changed. Mutation checks and the quick gate were not run because no fix was made.\nThe issue remains open for the next worker.\n\nInitial builds hit a sandbox denial in the inherited sccache C wrapper.\nClearing RUSTC_WRAPPER and CC in the command process allowed the tests to run.\nThe first commit command lacked an author identity. A command-local Git identity resolved it.\nNo global configuration changed.\nThe clean worktree remains at .claude/worktrees/issue-1580 for the next worker.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
